## Data Flow Diagram

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["host_state<br/>(host local x,y,θ,v,a)"] --> REL["Relative Measurement<br/>[distance, |Δv|]"]
    B["target_data<br/>(V2V received)"] --> REL
    
    REL --> GS["gamma_self<br/>exp(-e'·Tau⁻¹·e)"]
    C["host_target_estimate<br/>(host global est of target)"] --> GS
    
    REL --> GLP["gamma_local_peer<br/>exp(-Σ e_j'·Tau⁻¹·e_j)"]
    D["neighbor_estimates<br/>(neighbors' global est of target)"] --> GLP
    E["neighbor_host_estimates<br/>(neighbors' global est of host)"] --> GLP
    
    C --> GH["gamma_host<br/>exp(-Σ Mahal(host, neigh_j))"]
    D --> GH
    
    GH --> DT["DT = γ_host × γ_local_peer"]
    GLP --> DT
    GS -.->|"if γ_self < threshold"| DT
```

## MATLAB↔Python Mapping

| MATLAB | Python | Method |
|---|---|---|
| `gamma_cross = exp(-D)` | `gamma_host = exp(-d_host_total)` | Full-state Σ² Mahalanobis |
| `gamma_local = exp(-E)` | `gamma_local_peer = exp(-d_local_total)` | Relative τ² Mahalanobis |
| `gamma_local_our_self = exp(-E)` | `gamma_self = exp(-d_self)` | Relative τ² Mahalanobis |
| `tau2_matrix_gamma_local` | `distributed_local_tau2_diag` | `[1.5, 0.5]` = [distance, velocity] |

## Future Extension
The [_compute_relative_measurement()](file:///c:/Users/Quang%20Huy%20Nugyen/Desktop/PHD_paper/Simulation/QCAR/QCar2_Cran/Development/multi_vehicle_self_driving_RealQcar/qcar/Observer/TrustbasedDistributedObserver/trust_model.py#885-911) method currently builds a "fake sensor" from V2V data. When real LiDAR/radar ranging is available, replace its body with actual sensor readings — no other changes needed.
